\newlabel{fig:scalinglaw}{{1.5}{23}{The scaling law $D_3(3^k \cdot n) = D_3(n)$ illustrated with $n = 5$. Multiplying by powers of 3 appends zeros to the ternary representation, leaving the digital sum unchanged. This property is fundamental to the fractal structure of $D_3(n)$}{figure.1.5}{}}
